<title>INDONESIA: Bank Indonesia drains 52 bln rph temporarily.</title>
<headline>Bank Indonesia drains 52 bln rph temporarily.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's central bank, Bank Indonesia, drained some 52 billion rupiah temporarily from the money market early on Wednesday, money traders said.</p>
<p>The withdrawal was done through some 263 billion rupiah of short-term securities (SBPUs) due today and 231 billion rupiah of weekly central bank certificates (SBIs) to be settled today against some 20 billion rupiah of maturing SBIs.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364.</p>
</text>
